[CENTER][SIZE=5][B]🚇 1.0.0.2 — Live web map[/B][/SIZE]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdreval/MTR-Dynmap-Bridge/main/docs/images/web-map-overview.jpg[/IMG]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdreval/MTR-Dynmap-Bridge/main/docs/images/station-popup.jpg[/IMG]  [IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdreval/MTR-Dynmap-Bridge/main/docs/images/web-map-line-highlight.jpg[/IMG][/CENTER]

[LIST]
[*][B]🗺️ Live web map[/B] — open [B]http://<server-ip>:25970/[/B] or type [B]/mtrmap[/B]: every MTR rail (with curves) in the colours of your lines, platforms, depot sidings, station areas and depots.
[*][B]🚆 Moving vehicles[/B] — trains, boats, cable cars and airplanes move smoothly on the map, in their line's colour.
[*][B]🚉 Station window[/B] — lines, vehicles at the station and vehicles heading there (distance, speed), updated live.
[*][B]☑️ Transport type switches[/B] — hide trains, boats, cable cars or airplanes with one tick.
[*][B]🎨 Lines list[/B] — click a line to highlight it; [B]🔎 vehicle list[/B] with search and "follow".
[*][B]⚡ Light on the server[/B] — data is read on MTR's own simulation thread, the Minecraft thread is never used.
[*][B]📍 Dynmap optional[/B] — markers work exactly as before; sync interval and icons are now configurable.
[*][B]🇬🇧 / 🇷🇺[/B] English and Russian interface.
[*][B]🛠️ New:[/B] /mtrmap, /mtrstations, /mtrroutes, stations.txt / routes.txt exports, station and route blacklists.
[/LIST]

[B]Upgrade:[/B] replace the jar with 1.0.0.2 (keep your config.yml — new settings are added automatically), open TCP port 25970 and restart the server.
